<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RBM mode's gear for Commander Battle's Aserai troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_aserai.xml), read by
  CommanderBattle/RbmLoadouts.cs (the format is in its header). Light mode keeps the classes' mp_ gear and never reads
  this file. Same rules as the mp_ characters (cb_mpcharacters_aserai.xml):
  - Bots draw every slot from a random roster, so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters
    vary the looks (armour and helmets of one tier, shields of one size and kind), never the loadout.
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon, Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm, Item3 the horse archers' targe or the foot
    archers' second quiver. No Cape slot except the general's, as in the mp_ data. Mounted classes have a horse and a
    harness in the hero and every roster; foot classes have none.
  - Setups mirror the class's weapon setup perks by index (index 0, the class's own loadout, has none): the same slots,
    with the closest singleplayer item of the same weapon class. Sidearm rule as in the mp_ data: spears, lances and
    jereeds keep the sword; maces, swords and the swung tabar and executioner axe clear it; two-handers clear the shield.
  - Doctrine: javelin skirmishers on foot and horseback, tabar axemen and strong bows, in lighter armour; no pikes, no
    crossbows. Throwing weapons only in the skirmisher setups (RBM's jereeds and mahogany javelins, Javelin template).
  - Quivers: every RBM quiver holds 30, so the mp_ "large quiver" (50) is two quivers (Item1 and Item3) and the strong
    recurve setups, which use a regular quiver, clear Item3.
  - Gear tiers: light = levy (padded robes and leather strips, a steel desert helmet, a wooden oval shield, a proper
    weapon and a sidearm); medium = footmen (robes over mail, southern chain mail, helmets with mail); heavy = mamelukes
    (reinforced southern mail and scale on chain, brass closed or noble helmets, mail mittens, the best Aserai weapons).
    A step lighter than Vlandia and Sturgia at each weight.
  - Items only from the singleplayer and RBM item files that RBM.Multiplayer loads (RBM's versions carry RBM's stats),
    mostly the ids RBM's troop overhaul (RBMXML/RBMCombat_unit_overhaul.xml) gives these troops. No mp_ items.
  - No item on one of RBM's own holsters (RBM adds them in singleplayer only; the engine throws spawning it): the
    horse archers' targe is battania_shield_targe_a, not RBM's forearm battania_targe_b.
  - Seeded from RBM's overhaul:
      mp_light_infantry_aserai (tribal spearman)        aserai_tribesman, aserai_recruit
      mp_skirmisher_aserai (footman, medium infantry)   aserai_infantry, aserai_footman, aserai_mameluke_axeman (tabar)
      mp_shock_infantry_aserai (mameluke guard)         aserai_veteran_infantry, aserai_mameluke_guard
      mp_light_ranged_aserai (tribal archer)            aserai_skirmisher, aserai_archer (strong bow)
      mp_heavy_ranged_aserai (master archer)            aserai_master_archer, aserai_archer
      mp_light_cavalry_aserai (faris)                   aserai_tribal_horseman, aserai_faris, aserai_youth
      mp_heavy_cavalry_aserai (mameluke cavalry)        aserai_vanguard_faris, aserai_veteran_faris
      cb_light_horse_archer_aserai (bedouin)            aserai_mameluke_cavalry (weapons), aserai_skirmisher (armour)
      cb_general_aserai (emir and ghulams)              aserai_vanguard_faris, mamluke_palace_guard (armour)
  - Aserai have one couchable lance (aserai_lance_1_t5, the Mamluke Lance): both cavalry weights and the general carry
    it; the weights differ in armour, shield, sidearm and horse.
-->
